# Item icons. Referenced by `item.icon` (a lenient `ref?(sprite)`), so an item
# with no entry here still renders — it falls back to its flat `color` swatch,
# which is what all 66 items had before this file existed.
#
# ---- THE GRAIN --------------------------------------------------------------
# One art pixel is one world cell everywhere else in this game, and an icon has
# no world to be measured against — but it is drawn NEXT TO the hotbar swatches
# and, for a placeable, next to the block it puts down. So the icons are
# authored at the same coarseness on purpose: 2x2 for anything whose identity is
# a colour and a rough mass (ore, bar, gel, flask), 3x3 only where a SHAPE is
# the identity (a pickaxe is a head and a handle; a ladder is rails and rungs;
# an arrow is a head, a shaft and fletching). Nothing needs more than nine
# pixels, and everything that tried to use more stopped reading as part of the
# same game.
#
# ---- WHY ONE `icon_block_cube` FOR TWO DOZEN ITEMS --------------------------
# Roughly twenty-four items are `category placeable` and differ from each other
# in exactly one respect: which block they put down. Twenty-four hand-drawn
# cubes would be twenty-four copies of the same three-tone lump, and the moment
# one of them was redrawn the set would start to drift. They share this one
# sprite instead, drawn in a NEUTRAL grey specifically so a multiplicative tint
# by the item's own `color` lands where it should — which is the natural next
# step for the HUD, and is the same trick MobSprite's VARIANT_TINT already uses
# to make a crowd of one species read as individuals.
#
# ---- SHAPE VOCABULARY -------------------------------------------------------
# Repeated deliberately, so a glance at a slot says what KIND of thing is in it
# before it says which one:
#
#   diagonal metal + rock checker   ore, unsmelted
#   trapezoid, lit top              a bar
#   flask (narrow neck, wide body)  anything with a `use.effect`
#   bowl (mass over a rim)          anything that only heals
#   head-over-shaft                 a tool or a torch
#
# Colours are lifted from the item's own `color` so the icon and the fallback
# swatch are the same object at two resolutions.

# =============================================================================
# The shared placeable cube
# =============================================================================
# Lit from the upper left, which is where every other lit edge in this game
# comes from (see `edge` in content/blocks/*.block).
@sprite icon_block_cube
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #55555c #9a9aa4 #c8c8d2
seq |
  33
  21

# =============================================================================
# Tools — the progression ladder, and the icons the player stares at longest
# =============================================================================
# One shape, five metals. The pickaxe is the only item in the game whose tiers
# are a ladder the player is consciously climbing, so the tiers differ ONLY in
# the metal tones and the silhouette is identical across all five: what you are
# meant to read off the slot is "which metal", not "which shape".
#
#   row 0   the head — shade, lit crown, shade
#   row 1   the haft, under the head
#   row 2   the haft again, stepped right, so the handle reads as raked back

@sprite icon_pick_traveler
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #6b4a2c #6e6458 #a89a86
seq |
  232
  .1.
  ..1

@sprite icon_pick_copper
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #6b4a2c #a35f36 #e08a52
seq |
  232
  .1.
  ..1

@sprite icon_pick_iron
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #6b4a2c #7e7a78 #c8c4c0
seq |
  232
  .1.
  ..1

@sprite icon_pick_gold
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #6b4a2c #b08a2e #f0d878
seq |
  232
  .1.
  ..1

# The gem pick breaks the palette rule the other four keep — a dark violet haft
# instead of wood — because it is the end of the ladder and the only one that is
# not a stick with a rock on it.
@sprite icon_pick_gem
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #4a2c3a #8e2f5e #e878b4
seq |
  232
  .1.
  ..1

# =============================================================================
# Weapons
# =============================================================================
# Blade on the rising diagonal, hilt in the bottom-left corner. Three pixels of
# blade is enough to say "sword" as long as the guard breaks the line.

@sprite icon_sword_traveler
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #5a4630 #c2c6ce #8a8e96
seq |
  ..2
  .2.
  31.

# The King's Sword gets a fourth colour for the gem in the guard and a brighter
# tip than its own blade tone, so at three pixels it still reads as the relic
# rather than as a yellow traveler sword.
@sprite icon_sword_king
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #4a3a1e #f2dc94 #fff6cc #e0508c
seq |
  ..3
  .2.
  41.

# The bow is the one icon whose silhouette does all the work: columns 0 and 1
# carry the limb as a `(` curve and column 2 is the string drawn straight, so
# the two shapes cannot be confused with each other at three pixels wide.
@sprite icon_bow
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #d8c898 #8a5c2e
seq |
  .21
  2.1
  .21

@sprite icon_sling
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #b8a884 #7c7a78
seq |
  1.1
  .1.
  .2.

# Ammunition reads as a rising diagonal with a heavy end and a light end —
# fletching bottom-left, head top-right. The two tiers differ only in the head,
# which is exactly the difference that matters.
@sprite icon_arrow
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #d8cfae #a0783f #6e6c74
seq |
  ..3
  .2.
  1..

@sprite icon_arrow_iron
cellsW    3
cellsH    3
pal       . #d8cfae #a0783f #c8ccd4
seq |
  ..3
  .2.
  1..

# =============================================================================
# Ore, bars and stones
# =============================================================================
# ORE is the checker: two rock pixels and two metal pixels on the diagonal, so
# a vein reads as metal IN something rather than as a lump of metal. That is the
# same idea `texture speckle` carries on the ore blocks themselves.

@sprite icon_ore_copper
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #6e6a64 #a35f36 #e08a52
seq |
  13
  21

@sprite icon_ore_iron
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #6e6a64 #8e8a86 #cfcbc6
seq |
  13
  21

@sprite icon_ore_gold
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #6e6a64 #b08a2e #f0d878
seq |
  13
  21

# Coal is not a vein, it is a lump, so it gets the solid three-pixel mass
# instead of the checker — the shape difference is what stops a dark ore icon
# and a coal icon being the same picture.
@sprite icon_coal
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #1e1c20 #3a3640 #5a5464
seq |
  23
  12

# BARS are a trapezoid: a lit top face narrower than the body. Three pixels, but
# the missing top-left corner is the whole read.
@sprite icon_bar_copper
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #a35f36 #e08a52
seq |
  .2
  11

@sprite icon_bar_iron
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #8e8a86 #cfcbc6
seq |
  .2
  11

@sprite icon_bar_gold
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #b08a2e #f0d878
seq |
  .2
  11

# Cut stones are small on purpose: three pixels with the bright facet up and to
# the right, against the bar's three pixels with the light face flat on top.
@sprite icon_gem
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #6e1e46 #b8407e #f0a0d0
seq |
  .3
  12

@sprite icon_crystal_shard
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #4a3a7a #8e6ce0 #cfb4ff
seq |
  .3
  21

@sprite icon_flint
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #3e3c42 #6e6c74 #a8a6b0
seq |
  .2
  31

# =============================================================================
# Consumables
# =============================================================================
# FLASK = narrow neck over a wide body, and it is reserved for the three
# DRAUGHTS — the items whose whole reason to exist is a `use.effect` and which
# heal nothing at all, or nearly nothing. Food that carries an effect as a rider
# (spore cake) stays food-shaped, because what the player needs off the slot is
# "can I eat this", and the tooltip is right there for the rest.

@sprite icon_flask_fire
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #e8763a #ffc06a
seq |
  .2
  11

@sprite icon_flask_light
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #b48ad8 #f0d8ff
seq |
  .2
  11

@sprite icon_flask_haste
cellsW    2
cellsH    2
pal       . #8a72b8 #cfc0f0
seq |
  .2
  11

